{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Augmentation Placement.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Augmentation Placement.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"augmentation placement augmentation placement","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Augmentation Placement.md","fileName":"Augmentation Placement.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Augmentation Placement","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Tangible and Multimodal Interaction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Tangible and Multimodal Interaction","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Augmentation Placement.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Augmentation Placement.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"augmentation placement augmentation placement","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Augmentation Placement.md","fileName":"Augmentation Placement.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Augmentation Placement","heading":"Augmentation Placement","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Augmentation placement describes where generated output appears relative to the user and physical environment. Information may be attached to a world location, an object, the user's body, a display surface, or a moving region controlled by the user.\n\nPlacement affects meaning as well as visibility. A world-fixed label identifies a place, an object-fixed overlay follows its referent, and a view-fixed control remains available but no longer claims a physical location.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Tangible and Multimodal Interaction","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Augmentation Placement.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Augmentation Placement.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","source